          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
            is, a priori, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+invariant"} homotopy invariant
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framed+bordism+ring"} framed bordism ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
            turns out to equal the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+class"} Todd class
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coboundary"} cobounding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28U%2Cfr%29-manifold"} (U,fr)-manifold
            (
            %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66
            ).
          %h2#preliminaries Preliminaries
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In generalization to how the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-bordism+ring"} U-bordism ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^U_{2k}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+classes"} homotopy classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maps"} maps
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MU"} MU
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28U%2Cfr%29-bordism+ring"} (U,fr)-bordism ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi fr
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{U,fr}_{2k}
              is represented by maps into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+spaces"} quotient spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi MU
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} MU_{2k}/S^{2k}
              (for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mi Th
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Th
