          #TheProof.proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The first step in the proof of
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ToddClassesOnShortExactSequenceOfUFrBordismRings"} (3)
              is the observation (
              %a{:href => "#ConnerFloyd66"}> Conner-Floyd 66, p. 100-101
              ) that the representing map
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:InTermsOfHomotopyGroupsOfQuotientedThomSpace"} (1)
              for a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28U%2Cfr%29-manifold"} (U,fr)-manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{2k}
              cobounding a
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Fr
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fr
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is given by the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
              (see also at
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant"} Hopf invariant
                  –
                  %a{:href => "Hopf+invariant#InGeneralizedCohomology"} In generalized cohomology
            %div{:style => "margin: -20px 0px 20px 20px"}
              %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
                %img{:alt => "homotopy pasting diagram exhibiting cobounding UFr-manifolds", :src => "/nlab/files/CoboundingUFrManifoldDiagrammatically.jpg", :width => "470px"}/
                %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                  from
                  %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/schreiber/show/Equivariant+Cohomotopy+and+Oriented+Cohomology+Theory"} SS21
            %p
              From this, Conner-Floyd conclude essentially by considering the following
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+diagram"} homotopy
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pasting+diagram"} pasting diagram
              (the diagrammatic perspective here follows
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/M-Theory+as+Mf-Theory"} SS21
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Adams+e-invariant#ConstructionViaUnitCofiberTheories"} Adams e-invariant via unit cofiber theories
            %svg{:height => "304.564pt", :version => "1.1", :viewbox => "0 0 365.362 304.564", :width => "365.362pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
              %defs
                %g
                  %symbol#177592894-glyph0-0{:overflow => "visible"}
