            %p
              Here for the identification of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Todd+class"} Todd class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Td
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Td
              in the bottom of the diagram we used that
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/the+rational+Todd+class+is+the+Chern+character+of+the+Thom+class"} the rational Todd class is the Chern character of the Thom class
            %p
              That this Todd class equals the
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Q%2FZ"} Q/Z
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
              follows now since the latter is the top-degree component of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
              of any
              = succeed "-class" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+topological+K-theory"} complex topological K-theory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{2n} \coloneqq \sigma \circ c
              lifting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∈
